Subject: [PATCH] Exclusive full screen at the start stays exclusive with GL's own swap (TODO 442)

A player's laptop started in exclusive full screen (PS2X_FULLSCREEN=2) showed the picture in the lower right of the
screen with the desktop around it, every start since 0.8.7; switching to exclusive full screen in the game worked.
Patch 1007 sets VSync's window flag on GL's swap's first picture (SetWindowState(FLAG_VSYNC_HINT)), and raylib's
SetWindowState toggles exclusive full screen whenever the window's FLAG_FULLSCREEN_MODE differs from the flags it is
given (its one state check without "and it was asked for"): the window just put in exclusive full screen at the start
left it again at once, back at its windowed place with the screen's size. In the game the flag was set long before,
so a switch there was never undone. The window's own full screen bit is now passed along with VSync's flag. The same
call on Linux (its GL swap's VSync, older) had the same effect and goes through the same helper.

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_host_present.cpp b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_host_present.cpp
index 737dde6..a0f07ef 100644
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_host_present.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_host_present.cpp
@@ -278,6 +278,24 @@ namespace ps2_host_present
         g_drawing = true;
     }
 
+    namespace
+    {
+        // (TODO 442) VSync's flag set without leaving exclusive full screen. raylib's SetWindowState toggles exclusive full
+        // screen whenever the window's FLAG_FULLSCREEN_MODE differs from the flags it is given (its one state check without
+        // "and it was asked for"), so SetWindowState(FLAG_VSYNC_HINT) alone, on GL's swap's first picture, took a window
+        // just put in exclusive full screen at the start straight out of it again: the window went back to its windowed
+        // place at the screen's size (a player's picture in the lower right with the desktop around it). Switching in the
+        // game worked, as the flag was set by then. The window's own full screen bit is passed along, so nothing toggles.
+        // (SDL3's window has its own SetWindowState, which reads each flag given: VSync's alone there.)
+        void setVsyncFlag()
+        {
+            unsigned int flags = FLAG_VSYNC_HINT;
+            if (!ps2_platform::sdl3() && IsWindowState(FLAG_FULLSCREEN_MODE))
+                flags |= FLAG_FULLSCREEN_MODE;
+            SetWindowState(flags);
+        }
+    }
+
     void end()
     {
         if (!g_active)
@@ -291,7 +309,7 @@ namespace ps2_host_present
             {
                 applied = wanted;
                 if (wanted)
-                    SetWindowState(FLAG_VSYNC_HINT);
+                    setVsyncFlag();
                 else
                     ClearWindowState(FLAG_VSYNC_HINT);
             }
@@ -309,7 +327,7 @@ namespace ps2_host_present
             if (glSwapSync && wanted != applied)
             {
                 applied = wanted;
-                SetWindowState(FLAG_VSYNC_HINT);
+                setVsyncFlag();
                 if (!wanted)
                     ClearWindowState(FLAG_VSYNC_HINT);
                 std::fprintf(stderr, "[present] GL's own swap: VSync %s (swap interval %d)\n", wanted ? "on" : "off", wanted);
